**Stem Dry Matter Demands**

Demands for structural, metabolic and storage pools are provided to the organ arbitrator to simulate ongoing stem growth.  The demands for each dry matter pool are calculated as follows:

```
{[Cotton].Stem.PotentialGrowth}

// The fractional partitioning of this potential growth into structural, storage and metabolic pools is as follows:

{[Cotton].Stem.DMDemands.Structural}
{[Cotton].Stem.DMDemands.Structural.Fraction}

{[Cotton].Stem.DMDemands.Storage}
{[Cotton].Stem.DMDemands.Storage.StorageFraction}

{[Cotton].Stem.DMDemands.Metabolic}


```

The fraction of daily growth partitioned to stems is specified as a function of growth stage.

{[Cotton].Stem.PotentialGrowth.PartitionFraction}

**Stem Nitrogen Demand and Allocation**

Stem Nitrogen allocation to structural, storage and metabolic biomass pools is calculated by the OrganArbitrator as described above.  The stem model calculates the demands for each of these pools from information on the minimum, critical and maximum stem Nitrogen concentration for each predicted stage of development.

The minimum stem nitrogen concentration is used to describe the nitrogen content of the structural stem material. The difference between minimum and critical nitrogen concentration is assumed to correspond to metabolic stem material.  Storage nitrogen is equated with the difference between maximum and critical nitrogen concentrations.  The values of each of these is specified as follows.

```
// minimum and critical are set to be equal to provide a configuration where stem N is held in structural and storage pools only.
{[Cotton].Stem.MinimumNConc}
{[Cotton].Stem.CriticalNConc}
```
Storage N is parameterised therefore as the difference between minimum/critical N concentration and the following maximum N concentration.
{[Cotton].Stem.MaximumNConc}

**Senescence and Detachment**

Stem senescence can be specified to occur at differing rates before and after cutout.  

```
{[Cotton].Stem.SenescenceRate}

{[Cotton].Stem.DetachmentRateFunction}

```

where

Name | Description | Units
-|-|-
SenescenceRate | Fraction of live stem that senesces on the current day | /day
DetachmentRate | Fraction of dead stem that detaches on the current day | /day

**DM and N reuse within the plant**

Non-structural DM and N (ie storage or metabolic pools) can be available for reuse elsewhere within the plant to meet other demands via reallocation of DM or N from senescing biomass or retranslocation from live biomass during some growth phases (e.g. reallocation of N from senescing stem or retranslocation from stem N storage to support daily growth.  The potential fraction of DM or N that is available on any day is specified as follows:

```
{[Cotton].Stem.DMRetranslocationFactor}
{[Cotton].Stem.DMReallocationFactor}
{[Cotton].Stem.NRetranslocationFactor}
{[Cotton].Stem.NReallocationFactor}

```

**Seed Dry Matter Demands**

Demands for DM growth is only for structural growth (ie no storage or metabolic demand).

```
{[Cotton].Seed.DMDemandFunction.BollFilling}
```

where

```
{[Cotton].Seed.DMDemandFunction.BollFilling.HIDemand.HarvestIndexIncrease}
OutstandingHarvestIndex = Max (Increase, 0.0)
Increase = [Seed].PotentialHarvestIndex - [Seed].HarvestIndex
{[Cotton].Seed.DMDemandFunction.BollFilling.HIDemand.HarvestIndexIncrease.TTRemaining}
{[Cotton].Seed.PotentialHarvestIndex}
```

**Seed Nitrogen Demand and Allocation**

Seed Nitrogen allocation to structural, storage and metabolic biomass pools is calculated by the OrganArbitrator as described above.  The seed model calculates the demands for each of these pools from information on the minimum, critical and maximum seed Nitrogen concentration for each predicted stage of development.

The minimum seed nitrogen concentration is used to describe the nitrogen content of the structural seed material. The difference between minimum and critical nitrogen concentration is assumed to correspond to metabolic seed material.  Storage nitrogen is equated with the difference between maximum and critical nitrogen concentrations.  The values of each of these is specified as follows.

Minimum and critical are set to be equal to provide a configuration where Seed N is held in structural and storage pools only.  Storage N is parameterised therefore as the difference between minimum/critical N concentration and the following maximum N concentration.

{[Cotton].Seed.MinimumNConc}
{[Cotton].Seed.MaximumNConc}

